he source describes the mnemonic as a group of easy to remember letters, not words.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-003\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"generating the mnemonic and converting it into a ASCII seed\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source says the mnemonic is converted into an ASCII seed, not a binary seed.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-004\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source supports using the seed for BIP-0032 wallets, but it calls that seed ASCII rather than binary, which conflicts with the claim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-005\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-006\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-007\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source says computer-generated determinism, not randomness.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-008\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet süeed.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this, with a misspelling of seed.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-009\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets)\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_a.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-010\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"The demonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source says a multiple of 23 bits, not 32.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-011\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"With more entropy security is improved\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-012\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"but the sentence length increases\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states that more entropy increases sentence length.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-013\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-014\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source gives 1024-2048 byts, not 128-256 bits.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-015\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"First, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-016\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA652 hash.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source names the hash SHA652, not SHA256.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-017\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"This checksum is appended to the start of the initial entropy.\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source says the checksum goes at the start, not the end.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-018\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"these concatenated bits are split into groups of 12 bits\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source text says groups of 12 bits, not 11.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-019\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"split into groups of 12 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The 0-2047 range matches, but the source says each group is 12 bits, not 11.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-020\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"serving as an index into a wordlist\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states the numbers serve as wordlist indexes; the group bit-width discrepancy is covered under M-018.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-021\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Finally, we convert these numbers into words\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states the numbers are converted into words; the bit-width discrepancy is covered under M-018.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-022\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-023\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"CS = ENT / 32\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source gives this formula.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-024\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"MS = (ENT + CS) / 11\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The source gives this formula, with MS defined as sentence length in words.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-025\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The table row matches the claim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-026\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The table row matches the claim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-027\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The table row matches the claim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-028\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\",\"evidence_source\":\"source_b.md\",\"rationale\":\"The table row matches the claim.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"M-029\",\"verdict\":\"SUP